# Story page: bramble
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = Bramblewood
---
Beyond the quarry stood a wood where nothing was quite friendly, least of all the plants.

The brambles did not move while {name} watched them. They moved while {name} was busy, which is the habit of all the worst things, and the reason I never turn my back on a hedge.

Someone had left a pair of shears by the path. {name} found that snipping off half of oneself was surprisingly freeing. I would not recommend it to people. Snakes are different. Snakes grow back.
